WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680
High in the sky, cosmic rays hit
the upper atmosphere and make muons.

2
00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.530
A muon at rest has a
half-life of 1.5 microseconds.

3
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.050
Even falling at nearly the speed of light,

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.210
in that time it covers only about 450 m.

5
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.380
Without relativity, almost none
should survive the trip down.

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.220
Yet detectors at sea level count many.

7
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.390
Why do so many arrive?

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.860
In this mission, you'll find out what
changes when a particle moves at nearly

9
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.320
the speed of light.

10
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.050
Then you'll treat the
muons as an experiment,

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.460
and use their counts as evidence.

12
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: explain why so
many muons arrive at sea level.
